WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.780
AMANDA GORMAN: No matter who
you are, learning about poetry

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:06.180
is a huge source of power.

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:11.560
You too can write words that
will set the world on fire.

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:14.680
We braved the
belly of the beast,

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:18.210
We've learned that quiet
isn't always peace.

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:20.640
And the norms and
notions of what

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:24.150
"just is," isn't always justice.

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:31.800
You're going to learn not
only how to be a great poet

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.730
but how to be a changemaker.

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:41.240
When I was first writing poems,
what made them so special to me

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:46.430
was that experience of having my
feelings articulated and named

00:00:46.430 --> 00:00:47.330
on the page.

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:50.510
I could verbalize what
was going on in here

00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:51.650
that people didn't know.

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:54.110
For there is always
light if only

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:57.470
we're brave enough
to see it, if only

00:00:57.470 --> 00:01:00.050
we're brave enough to be it.

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:05.580
You should write at
least once every day.

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:06.640
You can write gibberish.

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:08.310
You can draw scarecrows.

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:09.570
Like, you can do whatever.

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:11.100
Just get your pen moving.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:14.580
I'm going to be sharing
ugly drafts of my own poems

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:16.830
and show you what
it means to perform

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:18.010
in front of an audience.

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:21.900
Trying to be heard but these
words don't sound right.

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:25.770
Could I ever be
in the spotlight?

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:28.350
When I was little, I
had a speech impediment,

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:31.800
which made it very difficult
for me to speak up for myself.

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:34.500
A lot of my first few
poems were about what

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:37.290
it was like to be lonely,
because I might not

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:41.010
look or speak like the
students around me.

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:43.200
There's always another
story to write,

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.750
always another verse
waiting on the horizon.

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:48.060
We all can harness
the power of poetry

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:50.520
to become stronger
communicators,

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:55.760
better leaders, and also
more compassionate people.

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:59.460
I'm Amanda Gorman, and
this is MasterClass.

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:01.806
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:08.600
I want to be the
teacher I never had.

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:10.500
[MUSIC PLAYING]

